course: dictionary
lesson: 584
title: Automated: done by machines
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Automated means done by machines or computers instead of people. When you meet this word, look at the words around it for clues. «The shop has automated checkouts» tells you that the shop uses machines to take payments, so you may not need to speak to a person.
explain: Auto is a clue inside the word. It comes from a Greek word meaning self, so something automated works by itself, without a person pressing every button. Automatic is a close word with a similar idea.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it in. «Automated doors open for you» still makes sense if you think "doors that open by machine," so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Automated means done by machines or computers instead of people.
fact: Automated is the past form of automate, so you may also see automate, automates and automating.
fact: Common phrases include fully automated, automated system and automated message.
fact: «Automated phone calls, or robocalls, use recorded or AI voices; some are surveys and some are scams.»
fact: A scam is a trick to cheat people, so always be careful with automated calls you did not ask for.
exercise: «The shop has automated checkouts, so you can pay without speaking to anyone.» What does automated mean here? | *Done by machines instead of people | Closed for the night | Done slowly by a group of children | Painted bright red
exercise: Which of these is an automated door? | A door that a teacher opens for the class every morning | A heavy wooden door opened with a big key | *A door that opens by itself when a sensor sees you
exercise: Find and copy the word from «Automated phone calls, or robocalls, use recorded or AI voices» that names calls made by machines. | *robocalls | recorded | voices | AI
test:
test: What is a scam? | *A trick to cheat people | A kind of party game | A friendly surprise | A type of weather
test: Why might a factory be fully automated? | Nothing is ever made there | Workers sing all day long | *Machines do the work instead of people | Only people are allowed to use the machines
exam: Which is the best example of an automated message? | A note passed between two friends | A letter a teacher writes by hand to one child | *A text sent by a computer to thousands of phones | A song sung together in assembly
